WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.268 --> 00:00:03.736
-Republicans passed a sweeping
overhaul of the tax code

00:00:03.736 --> 00:00:06.572
that will overwhelming benefit
corporations and the wealthy,

00:00:06.572 --> 00:00:09.942
amounting to nothing left than
a brazen heist of the country.

00:00:09.942 --> 00:00:12.078
For more on this,
it's time for "A Closer Look."

00:00:12.078 --> 00:00:16.816
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:00:16.816 --> 00:00:18.584
President Trump
keeps his insisting,

00:00:18.584 --> 00:00:20.320
despite all evidence
to the contrary,

00:00:20.320 --> 00:00:22.087
that this tax bill
will not be a boon

00:00:22.087 --> 00:00:23.289
to the richest Americans.

00:00:23.289 --> 00:00:25.825
In fact, in the spirit
of the holiday season,

00:00:25.825 --> 00:00:28.928
he keeps calling it a Christmas
gift to the middle class.

00:00:28.928 --> 00:00:31.230
-This is gonna be
one of the great gifts

00:00:31.230 --> 00:00:33.299
to the middle-income people
of this country

00:00:33.299 --> 00:00:35.201
that they've ever gotten
for Christmas.

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:38.504
It will be the greatest
Christmas present

00:00:38.504 --> 00:00:40.473
that a lot of people
have ever received.

00:00:40.473 --> 00:00:43.242
We're now one
huge step closer to delivering

00:00:43.242 --> 00:00:47.447
to the American people
the historic tax relief

00:00:47.447 --> 00:00:51.050
as a giant present
for Christmas.

00:00:51.050 --> 00:00:53.686
Remember I said
we're bringing Christmas back?

00:00:53.686 --> 00:00:55.588
Christmas is back,

00:00:55.588 --> 00:00:57.590
bigger and better
than ever before.

00:00:57.590 --> 00:00:59.358
We're bringing Christmas back.

00:00:59.358 --> 00:01:02.729
-It almost sounds like
he was about to start singing.

00:01:02.729 --> 00:01:03.730
[ Laughter ]

00:01:03.730 --> 00:01:05.565
It's like he's doing
a Weird Al cover

00:01:05.565 --> 00:01:07.934
of a Justin Timberlake song.

00:01:07.934 --> 00:01:10.102
"I'm bringing Christmas back.

00:01:10.102 --> 00:01:12.672
Them other holidays
are super whack."

00:01:12.672 --> 00:01:13.740
[ Laughter ]

00:01:13.740 --> 00:01:17.043
Also,
Christmas didn't go anywhere.

00:01:17.043 --> 00:01:19.345
We're all up to our necks
in Christmas.

00:01:19.345 --> 00:01:21.614
Every TV show
has a Christmas episode.

00:01:21.614 --> 00:01:23.783
Every commercial
has a Christmas song.

00:01:23.783 --> 00:01:27.086
There's a 70-foot tree
outside my office window,

00:01:27.086 --> 00:01:29.722
and every barista in town
is wearing antlers.

00:01:29.722 --> 00:01:32.358
If you want to bring
something back, try Kwanzaa.

00:01:32.358 --> 00:01:34.093
That thing
straight-up disappeared.

00:01:34.093 --> 00:01:35.528
[ Laughter ]

00:01:35.528 --> 00:01:38.331
Of course, virtually every
reputable study of the tax bill

00:01:38.331 --> 00:01:40.332
says the corporations
and the wealthy will benefit

00:01:40.332 --> 00:01:41.667
far more than anyone else.

00:01:41.667 --> 00:01:43.903
For one thing, the corporate
tax cuts are permanent,

00:01:43.903 --> 00:01:45.604
while the individual
tax cuts expire,

00:01:45.604 --> 00:01:47.707
which means that by 2027,

00:01:47.707 --> 00:01:51.444
more than 80% of the plan's
benefits go to the top 1%

00:01:51.444 --> 00:01:54.547
while 53% of taxpayers
will see a tax hike.

00:01:54.547 --> 00:01:56.148
And if you just
look at next year,

00:01:56.148 --> 00:01:57.717
the plan's benefits
are very heavily skewed

00:01:57.717 --> 00:01:58.951
towards the wealthy.

00:01:58.951 --> 00:02:01.788
Middle-income taxpayers
would pay about $900 less

00:02:01.788 --> 00:02:04.257
where the highest-income
1% of households

00:02:04.257 --> 00:02:07.594
would get an average tax cut
of roughly $50,000.

00:02:07.594 --> 00:02:09.129
Here's what that means
in real terms.

00:02:20.939 --> 00:02:22.675
So, to recap,
if you're rich,

00:02:22.675 --> 00:02:24.043
you're getting
a car for Christmas,

00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:27.079
and if you're not, go ahead
and wrap up a can of gas.

00:02:27.079 --> 00:02:28.747
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:02:28.747 --> 00:02:31.083
Of course, Republicans --

00:02:31.083 --> 00:02:33.586
Ooh.

00:02:33.586 --> 00:02:35.788
[ Laughter ]

00:02:35.788 --> 00:02:38.157
I'm gonna set this
next to the fire

00:02:38.157 --> 00:02:39.158
and open it later.

00:02:39.158 --> 00:02:42.428
[ Laughter ]

00:02:42.428 --> 00:02:45.264
Of course, Republicans can't
point to any actual proof

00:02:45.264 --> 00:02:47.467
their plan would benefit lower-
and middle-income people,

00:02:47.467 --> 00:02:49.736
so all they can do
is repeat vague talking points

00:02:49.736 --> 00:02:50.969
about improving the economy.

00:02:50.969 --> 00:02:53.172
For example, Ivanka Trump,
the President's daughter

00:02:53.172 --> 00:02:54.908
and adviser,
tweeted this week...

00:03:04.984 --> 00:03:07.553
Prompting a response
from her father, who wrote...

00:03:08.454 --> 00:03:11.024
Man, that's got to suck
for Eric and Don Jr.

00:03:11.024 --> 00:03:13.092
They tweet about their dad
all the time...

00:03:13.092 --> 00:03:14.393
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.393 --> 00:03:17.930
...and all they ever get
is a broken upside-down heart.

00:03:17.930 --> 00:03:20.132
[ Laughter ]

00:03:20.132 --> 00:03:22.268
"What's the button
for hate them?"

00:03:22.268 --> 00:03:23.736
[ Laughter ]

00:03:23.736 --> 00:03:26.072
And yet despite the overwhelming
evidence to the contrary,

00:03:26.072 --> 00:03:28.341
Trump has repeatedly claimed
not just that the wealthy,

00:03:28.341 --> 00:03:30.008
in general,
would be hurt by the bill,

00:03:30.008 --> 00:03:31.677
but that he personally
would pay more in taxes

00:03:31.677 --> 00:03:33.112
than he did before.

00:03:33.112 --> 00:03:36.682
-We're also going to eliminate
tax breaks and complex loopholes

00:03:36.682 --> 00:03:39.151
taken advantage of
by the wealthy.

00:03:39.151 --> 00:03:40.286
Who are they?
I don't...

00:03:40.286 --> 00:03:42.255
[ Laughter ]

00:03:42.255 --> 00:03:44.790
I think my accountants
are going crazy right now.

00:03:44.790 --> 00:03:47.059
It's all right.
Hey, look, I'm President.

00:03:47.059 --> 00:03:48.428
I don't care.

00:03:48.428 --> 00:03:51.130
I don't care anymore.
I don't care.

00:03:51.130 --> 00:03:53.466
-We definitely believe
that you don't care.

00:03:53.466 --> 00:03:54.734
[ Laughter ]

00:03:54.734 --> 00:03:59.472
You're, by far,
our most checked-out President.

00:03:59.472 --> 00:04:00.773
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:00.773 --> 00:04:05.445
I mean, James Garfield
worked harder than you

00:04:05.445 --> 00:04:07.080
<i> after</i> he was assassinated.

00:04:07.080 --> 00:04:08.347
[ Laughter ]

00:04:08.347 --> 00:04:10.983
You watch more TV than a
6th-grader at home with the flu.

00:04:10.983 --> 00:04:13.953
Trump watches so much TV,
we're like a week away

00:04:13.953 --> 00:04:16.222
from him tweeting
about "The Price is Right."

00:04:16.222 --> 00:04:22.428
[ Laughter ]

00:04:22.428 --> 00:04:23.796
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:04:23.796 --> 00:04:27.533
Now, obviously,
we can't know exactly

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:29.168
how Trump would benefit
from this bill,

00:04:29.168 --> 00:04:31.537
since he still refuses
to release his tax returns.

00:04:31.537 --> 00:04:33.639
But we do know
there are lots of changes

00:04:33.639 --> 00:04:34.840
that would impact him directly.

00:04:34.840 --> 00:04:36.376
For one thing,
Republicans lowered

00:04:36.376 --> 00:04:37.810
the top income-tax bracket.

00:04:37.810 --> 00:04:39.545
There are also tax breaks
for so-called

00:04:39.545 --> 00:04:42.648
pass-through businesses, which
includes the Trump organization.

00:04:42.648 --> 00:04:44.617
There was even
a last-minute provision added

00:04:44.617 --> 00:04:46.685
that specifically extends
a new tax break

00:04:46.685 --> 00:04:49.622
for pass-through businesses
to real-estate investors.

00:04:49.622 --> 00:04:50.956
In fact, the bill
has so many complicated

00:04:50.956 --> 00:04:52.325
tax breaks and giveaways,

00:04:52.325 --> 00:04:55.028
Republicans are trying to argue
that average Americans

00:04:55.028 --> 00:04:56.929
would benefit
from those tax breaks

00:04:56.929 --> 00:04:59.665
by really stretching the meaning
of the word "average."

00:04:59.665 --> 00:05:02.434
Take this tweet yesterday
from Texas Senator John Cornyn.

00:05:02.434 --> 00:05:04.470
Cornyn wrote...

00:05:21.487 --> 00:05:24.290
Yeah, you know,
that average American family

00:05:24.290 --> 00:05:27.593
that has two kids, a house,
a white picket fence,

00:05:27.593 --> 00:05:29.428
corporate income,
noncorporate business income,

00:05:29.428 --> 00:05:30.996
three limited-liability
corporations,

00:05:30.996 --> 00:05:32.932
two S corporations,
two C corporations,

00:05:32.932 --> 00:05:34.133
a commercial
real-estate venture,

00:05:34.133 --> 00:05:36.135
a limited-liability partnership,
carried interest,

00:05:36.135 --> 00:05:37.336
oh, and a dog.

00:05:37.336 --> 00:05:39.839
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:05:39.839 --> 00:05:43.709
Average.
You know, average.

00:05:43.709 --> 00:05:47.046
In fact, this bill doesn't even
deliver on the flimsy pretext

00:05:47.046 --> 00:05:48.880
Republicans initially gave
for their tax plan --

00:05:48.880 --> 00:05:50.282
simplifying the tax code.

00:05:50.282 --> 00:05:53.152
For example, the plan keeps
seven different tax brackets

00:05:53.152 --> 00:05:55.554
rather than the three
Republicans initially proposed.

00:05:55.554 --> 00:05:57.723
Former GOP presidential
candidate Herman Cain

00:05:57.723 --> 00:06:00.192
proposed his own tax-code
simplification plan,

00:06:00.192 --> 00:06:03.062
called the 9-9-9 plan,
was asked about that failure

00:06:03.062 --> 00:06:05.430
on Fox News
and didn't seem too troubled.

00:06:05.430 --> 00:06:07.033
-Your plan had 9-9-9.

00:06:07.033 --> 00:06:08.734
This one
still has seven brackets.

00:06:08.734 --> 00:06:11.270
It may not be
as simple as you wanted,

00:06:11.270 --> 00:06:14.006
but is it a big win
for Republicans?

00:06:14.006 --> 00:06:17.843
-It's not 9-9-9-,
but it's fine, fine, fine.

00:06:17.843 --> 00:06:19.912
-Look how happy Herman Cain is.

00:06:19.912 --> 00:06:22.114
He can't believe
they set him up for a rhyme.

00:06:22.114 --> 00:06:24.716
His public life is done.

00:06:24.716 --> 00:06:27.285
Now he'll just disappear,
never to be seen again.

00:06:27.285 --> 00:06:30.289
No, Herman, don't go!
What will we do without you?!

00:06:30.289 --> 00:06:33.893
-Don't worry.
You'll be fine, fine, fine.

00:06:33.893 --> 00:06:36.762
[ Laughter ]

00:06:36.762 --> 00:06:41.267
-And on top of everything else,

00:06:41.267 --> 00:06:45.104
this bill also adds nearly
$1.5 trillion to the deficit

00:06:45.104 --> 00:06:48.173
after years of GOP hysteria
about government spending,

00:06:48.173 --> 00:06:50.410
and Republicans
are already being very open

00:06:50.410 --> 00:06:52.111
about the fact
that they're going to use

00:06:52.111 --> 00:06:53.946
the deficits they created
as an excuse to cut

00:06:53.946 --> 00:06:55.614
Social Security, Medicare,
and Medicaid

00:06:55.614 --> 00:06:57.916
under the guise
of so-called welfare reform.

00:06:57.916 --> 00:07:00.453
Last week, House Speaker
Paul Ryan, a father of three,

00:07:00.453 --> 00:07:02.020
was asked about
paying for those programs

00:07:02.020 --> 00:07:04.190
and said the problem wasn't that
Republicans are giving away

00:07:04.190 --> 00:07:05.925
billions to corporations
and the wealthy

00:07:05.925 --> 00:07:08.427
but that people
aren't having enough babies.

00:07:08.427 --> 00:07:11.163
-The great thing about
tax reform coming right now

00:07:11.163 --> 00:07:13.799
is we're gonna be able
to create the kind of an economy

00:07:13.799 --> 00:07:16.201
that produces good,
family-supporting jobs,

00:07:16.201 --> 00:07:18.871
higher wages that
will be there for people

00:07:18.871 --> 00:07:21.373
who are stuck in poverty
and welfare to go to.

00:07:21.373 --> 00:07:24.243
This is going to be the new
economic challenge for America.

00:07:24.243 --> 00:07:25.477
People.

00:07:25.477 --> 00:07:28.213
Baby boomers are retiring.

00:07:28.213 --> 00:07:29.715
I did my part, but we need

00:07:29.715 --> 00:07:32.184
to have higher birth rates
in this country.

00:07:32.184 --> 00:07:34.586
-I'm sorry.
<i> You</i> did you your part?

00:07:34.586 --> 00:07:36.722
You know who might have
something to say about that?

00:07:36.722 --> 00:07:38.390
Your wife.

00:07:38.390 --> 00:07:40.759
If I had turned to my wife
right after my son was born

00:07:40.759 --> 00:07:42.294
and said,
"Well, I did my part,"

00:07:42.294 --> 00:07:44.530
I'm pretty sure,
she would've picked me up

00:07:44.530 --> 00:07:46.665
and broken me over her knee
like Bane.

00:07:46.665 --> 00:07:48.867
[ Laughter and applause ]

00:07:48.867 --> 00:07:50.903
It tells you everything you need
to know about the Trump era

00:07:50.903 --> 00:07:52.438
if this is how 2017 is ending,

00:07:52.438 --> 00:07:54.206
with Republicans
ransacking the country,

00:07:54.206 --> 00:07:55.540
taking healthcare
away from millions,

00:07:55.540 --> 00:07:57.810
and then telling women
that the solution is for them

00:07:57.810 --> 00:07:58.910
to have more babies.

00:07:58.910 --> 00:08:00.279
Working and middle-class people

00:08:00.279 --> 00:08:01.847
overwhelmingly
dislike this bill.

00:08:01.847 --> 00:08:03.516
Meanwhile,
corporations and the wealthy

00:08:03.516 --> 00:08:05.184
are looking at it
and saying it's...

00:08:05.184 --> 00:08:06.885
-Fine, fine, fine.

00:08:06.885 --> 00:08:08.587
-This has been "A Closer Look."

00:08:08.587 --> 00:08:12.191
[ Cheers and applause ]

